      "seconds": 22.17,
      "answer": "IVMS, or Integrated Vehicle Management System, is part of the vehicle telematics offerings within the NAVAS ecosystem. It includes core functionalities such as location tracking, trip history, and geofencing. Additional features can be enabled, such as driver behavior monitoring (ECO), business intelligence dashboards, and job scheduling/routing (JMS/GIS). The system is designed to provide stable tracking, compliance, and report readiness, with baseline alerts for overspeed, ignition on/off, geofence in/out, and towing (if supported).\n\nSource: NAVAS CMS User Manual — this is the documented design; I can't confirm from here which parts are live.",
