      "http_status": 200,
      "seconds": 20.48,
      "answer": "VEBA escrow holds a renter's payment in tokens when they book an asset, and releases it to the owner only once telematics proves the asset was used as agreed — engine hours, geofence-confirmed possession, duration, and usage class.\n\nA booking moves through reserved, active, and released states. It can also become disputed, refunded, or partially adjusted when the usage doesn't match the booking.\n\nSource: NAVAS Ecosystem Vision Scope Document — this is the documented design; I can't confirm from here which parts are live.",
